                <pb facs="0128" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119P43/856: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-05T12:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                                1919, noon.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>5557. For the Secretary of State from Polk:</p>
                <p>Your 3942 [<hi rendition="#italic">3941</hi>], December 2, 4 p.m. Arrangements
                    have been made with General Connor for holding the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >America</hi>. Mission will leave Paris in accordance with your instructions
                    on the evening of the 9th and we hope to sail from Brest on the 10th. Polk.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
